# Global UI catalog (cross-repo)

**SSOT on disk:** `/Users/Shared/Developer/cursor/ui-catalog/`  
**GitHub mirror:** `https://github.com/baturmont/ui-catalog`  
**Skill:** `ui-catalog` (read `WORKFLOW.md` and follow it)

## When this applies

Any frontend design, redesign, new page, component, landing, dashboard chrome, or mobile UI — in **any** repo or greenfield project.

## Agent must

1. Open the catalog (`README` → `INDEX` → `SOURCES` / `favorites`) **before** freehanding UI.
2. Detect or confirm **stack** (`STACK-FILTERS.md`): vanilla | vite-react | next | vue | mobile | …
3. Shortlist **2–3** real components with source URLs; recommend one.
4. Install via official path or port per workflow (no fake import paths).
5. Apply **repo brand/tokens only if that repo defines them** — catalog is not product-specific.
6. Optional **Superdesign** only **after** a catalog direction is chosen (variants of that direction).
7. Optional **ui-ux-pro-max** for a11y/touch/contrast — not a component store.

## Agent must not

- Invent a full button/sheet/nav system when the catalog covers it
- Drop React kits into vanilla HTML repos without an explicit stack migration
- Default to purple-gradient / Inter-only / glassmorphism clichés (`refs/anti-generic.md`)
- Skip source citation in the reply or PR

## Output

Use the shortlist table from `ui-catalog/WORKFLOW.md` when proposing UI.
